; Integer exponents now also flow through `pow64`'s log_inline + exp_inline
; (musl has no integer-exponent fast path), and still land exactly on the
; representable result. This path was already host-stable under `std.math.pow`
; (pure repeated squaring); pinning it guards the new routing against drift.
; Pinned decimals are the canonical `{d}` rendering.
(pow 2.0 10.0)
(pow 3.0 4.0)
